docs/review-tracking/raw/S1-base-63fab37.log:587:-- **Generic Alias Proxy**: Wraps generic aliases in a proxy that intercepts attribute access, checks if accessed attribute is one of the decorated takes_alias methods -- if so, pass in the proxy alias, otherwise retain normal behavior.
docs/review-tracking/raw/S1-base-63fab37.log:589:+- **Class-creation hook**: `@takes_alias` produces a *descriptor* — a subclass of `classmethod`. When its `__set_name__` runs as the owning class is created, the class's existing `__init_subclass__` and `__class_getitem__` are wrapped: `__init_subclass__` so the behavior is reinstalled on subclasses, and `__class_getitem__` so it returns a custom generic-alias proxy (a subclass of `typing._GenericAlias`) — except on pydantic models, which are left unmodified. A `TypeVarValue` descriptor triggers the same wrapping from *its* `__set_name__`, so a class can opt in via either.
docs/review-tracking/raw/S1-base-63fab37.log:590:+- **Generic-alias proxy**: wraps `Foo[int]`-style aliases in a proxy that intercepts attribute access — if the accessed attribute is one of the alias-aware descriptors (`@takes_alias` methods or `TypeVarValue`), it hands over the proxy alias; otherwise behavior is unchanged.
